Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:37:14

Breaking. The app is now called PS5 Core Unlock, before PS5 CPU Tools. It gets the step window of its twin in
bc250-bazzite. The window leads through five steps instead of opening a terminal: Scan, Test the stock cores, Unlock
and restart, Test the new cores, and Install. It runs ps5-cores-bisect.sh and ps5-cores-unlock.sh itself. Each step's
row says the one thing to do now, with its pill on that row, and a green bar says when you're finished. After the
unlock and between attempts the window restarts the board itself after a countdown. It opens again after the login
with the next step. A desktop notification says when a step ends. A test blocks sleep while it runs. After a full
power off in the middle of the test, step 4 turns the new cores on again with ps5-cores-unlock.sh --apply. Install
needs no restart, because the cores are on already. The window's Unattended and Auto resume switches are gone, and so
is the separate unlock part with its verdict row. The script's --auto still works from a terminal. Uninstall also
removes the window's autostart entry.

The bottom row holds the other pills on the left and the Details and Advanced pills at its right end. The window
always opens 900 pixels wide and fits its height to the page once it shows. The tooltips are rounded boxes on the
window's dark background, as in the suite's other apps.

ps5-cores-bisect.sh has two new options. --scan reads the presence mask, the cores and what a run needs, then exits
without writing to the SMU. --only ITEM runs only the attempts of one item. The help page lists them.

Every attempt could end as LOAD-FAIL with "temp-path '.' must be readable and writeable" when the test started from a
folder the script can't write. stress-ng 0.22 refuses to start there, even for its CPU stressors. ps5-cores-bisect.sh
now gives stress-ng the logs folder of its results as its temp folder.

The "Changes the board" text in the portal and the wiki chapter is rewritten to the writing standard. It now says that
the app restarts the board after the core unlock, and between rounds when Same boot is off, after a 15 second
countdown. The wiki chapter is the twin's, rewritten to the writing standard.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:58:22

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:31:05

Added. The controller works this app, as it works the portal: the app carries core's new exit_keys. The d-pad and the
left stick move the focus, A presses what has the focus, LB and RB change the tab, B closes the window and the touchpad
moves the mouse pointer.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Release 0.1.2.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 18:33:23

Fixed. The app's copy of core's exit_keys.py takes out the window class that pygame sets when it starts, as
core/bazzite_console_core/exit_keys.py does. A program the app starts no longer inherits it.
tools/tests/test_instance_copies.py checks that the copy matches core.

